      "text": "[inc 2691 shipping intlshippingslowdown > INC-2691: shipping elevated latency > Action items]\n1. Add a Grafana annotation and a low-urgency alert on `flagd_flag_evaluations_total` deltas, so a flag flip is visible on every dashboard. *(owner: platform-eng)*\n2. Add \"check the dependency graph before the service that paged\" as step 1 of the `checkout` runbook. *(owner: checkout)* \u2014 done, see `knowledge/runbook/checkout.md`.\n3. Confirm the `shipping` runbook's known-failure-modes section lists `intlShippingSlowdown` with this signature. *(owner: checkout)*"
    },
    {
      "ref": "doc:e2f0b141410f1946::0001::808f890ea039a90e",
      "title": "knowledge/runbook/checkout.docx",
      "doc_type": "runbook",
      "effective_date": "2026-09-26",
      "score": 3.2614,
      "text": "# checkout runbook\n\nThe synchronous order pipeline. Calls cart, currency, product-catalog, shipping, payment, then email, in order. Implemented in Go. Owned by the checkout team (PD-CHECKOUT, #astroshop-checkout).\n\n## When this fires\n\ncheckout is on the customer-facing critical path. A failure here surfaces on frontend, frontend-proxy as elevated errors or latency, often before a checkout alert fires. If you were paged for one of those and the cause is not obvious there, check checkout early.\n\n## Thresholds\n\n| Signal | Objective | Page at |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Availability (28d) | 99.5% | error budget 50% burned in 1h |\n| Duration p95 | < 1200 ms | > 1800 ms for 5m |\n| Duration p99 | < 2500 ms | > 3750 ms for 5m |\n\n## Dashboards and queries\n\nGrafana: the checkout row on the Astroshop service dashboard. The queries behind that row, for pasting straight into Prometheus:\n\npromql\n\n# error ratio (span metrics)\n\nsum(rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{service_name=\"checkout\", span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_SERVER\", status_code=\"STATUS_CODE_ERROR\"}[5m]))\n\n/ sum(rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{service_name=\"checkout\", span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_SERVER\"}[5m]))\n\n# p95 duration, ms (span metrics)\n\nhistogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(traces_span_metrics_duration_milliseconds_bucket{service_name=\"checkout\", span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_SERVER\"}[5m])))\n\n# rpc_server_call_duration_seconds p95\n\nhistogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(rpc_server_call_duration_seconds_bucket{service_name=\"checkout\"}"
    },
    {
      "ref": "doc:5cea1250b8e7b517::0000::e0a4d9db047c5eb5",
      "title": "knowledge/runbook/email.md",
      "doc_type": "runbook",
      "effective_date": "2026-09-26",
      "score": 3.0777,
      "text": "# email runbook\n\nSends the order-confirmation email. Called by checkout after the order is committed, best-effort. Implemented in Ruby. Owned by the checkout team (PD-CHECKOUT, #astroshop-checkout).\n\n## When this fires\n\n`email` is on the customer-facing critical path. A failure here surfaces on `checkout`, `frontend`, `frontend-proxy` as elevated errors or latency, often before a `email` alert fires. If you were paged for one of those and the cause is not obvious there, check `email` early.\n\n## Thresholds\n\n| Signal | Objective | Page at |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Availability (28d) | 99% | error budget 50% burned in 1h |\n| Duration p95 | < 1000 ms | > 1500 ms for 5m |\n\n## Dashboards and queries\n\nGrafana: the `email` row on the Astroshop service dashboard. The queries behind that row, for pasting straight into Prometheus:\n\n# error ratio (span metrics)\nsum(rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{service_name=\"email\", span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_SERVER\", status_code=\"STATUS_CODE_ERROR\"}[5m]))\n  / sum(rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{service_name=\"email\", span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_SERVER\"}[5m]))\n# p95 duration, ms (span metrics)\nhistogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(traces_span_metrics_duration_milliseconds_bucket{service_name=\"email\", span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_SERVER\"}[5m])))\n# demo_notification_confirmations_total rate\nsum(rate(demo_notification_confirmations_total{service_name=\"email\"}[5m]))\n# container_memory_usage_total_bytes\ncontainer_memory_usage_total_bytes{container_name=\"email\"}\n\nIn "
    }
  ],
